</li>

<li> '''[[#Roinn cainte / Part of speech|Part of speech]].''' <br />
<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
<li> '''Word.''' i.e. {{tmpl|pn}}</li>
<li> '''‘Form of’ link.'''</li>
</ol></ol>

The ‘form of’ templates state what the form is and link back to the main entry.

They start with a . (full stop / period) and are the same as the abbreviations used in the inflection templates, e.g. genitive singular appears in the inflection as ''gu.'' (''ginideach uatha'') so the ‘form of’ template is {{tmpl|.gu|}}.
</div>

